      en: "The Church of San Francisco de Borja in Santiago was built in 1618 as part of a Jesuit college. After the Jesuits' expulsion in 1767, it became a parish church. The baroque church has a rectangular floor plan and a bell tower. It houses an 18th-century altarpiece and a 19th-century organ. Declared a national monument in 1970, it is known for its carved pulpit and woodwork. Located in the city center, it remains an active place of worship.",
